  "instance_name": "mapping_001",
  "label": "The drag performer is mapped as the subject of the self-acceptance struggle",
  "description": "The text 'they want to be accepted for who they are, yet there aren't able to accept themselves for who they are' explicitly refers to 'they' as the subject of the internal conflict. The visual material, the drag performer, is the central entity depicted and is directly mapped onto this textual subject 'they'. The drag performer's confident external presentation (visual) contrasts with the internal struggle described in the text, establishing a clear analogical mapping where the performer embodies the 'they' in the text.",
